'''Vega''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Cat Capsules]] during [[Street Fighter Collaboration Event]]. He was added in [[Version 10.0 Update|Version 10.0]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 573
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Vega
|name2 = Vega CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Vega CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Vega is an Uber Rare that freezes [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies and sometimes delivers a [[Critical Hit]]. At first glance with his 100% freeze rate, 30% Critical chance and Long Distance ability, this unit may seem a very good [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal cat]] but it's not quite the case. Simply put, Long Distance has the purpose of making units good against backliners like [[Master A.]] as it allows them to pierce beyond the enemy frontline. This is however useless for Vega because no Metal backliners exist, meaning that only the negative aspect of him having a blind spot remains. On the bright side, his high knockback count nullifies this a bit.

This also means that without the support of good crowd-controllers such as the drops from the [[:Category:Cyclone Stages|Cyclone Stages]], Vega will only be able to hit his targets at most a couple times before they get too close. Additionally, his critical hit rate of 30% is not high enough to be relied upon without adequate protection.

Outside of his Metal niche, Vega is barely usable but not recommended, as his awful DPS usually prevents him from being worth bringing along.

{{Job|Classification = Critter & Crowd-Controller}}

