==Trivia==
*In Japan, and by extension [[Nyanko Daisensou|Nyanko Daisensou]], this Fighter is instead known as [[Balrog (Uber Rare Cat)|Balrog]], while Vega's name was originally assigned to [[M. Bison (Uber Rare Cat)|M. Bison]].
** This was likely done proactively when localizing Street Fighter II to avoid legal trouble from real life boxer Mike Tyson's legal team, though perhaps they say Bison's original name as not threatening enough to western players, and more fitting for the ego-drunk fighter.
*** The title "Boxer" ([[Balrog (Uber Rare Cat)|Balrog]]), "Claw" (Vega) and "Dictator" ([[M. Bison (Uber Rare Cat)|M. Bison]]) have been adopted to not cause confusion when referring to these three Shadaloo leaders between Japanese and international players.

